// De-risking test for `blockIdx` combined with num_blocks > 1: every kernel
// in this repo so far has used blockDim/threadIdx for parallelism with
// num_blocks=1 (a single block), so EXPR_BLOCK_IDX has only ever been
// exercised as "always 0" internally, never as a real per-block register
// read across multiple dispatched blocks. The upcoming DS-CNN depthwise/
// pointwise/maxpool kernels rely on `channel = blockIdx*4 + threadIdx` to
// parallelize across channel groups larger than one block's threadDim -- so
// this needs its own proof on real RTL before any conv kernel depends on it.
//
// Launch with num_blocks=4, blockDim=4 (16 threads total, matching the
// depthwise block0 channel count C=16): each thread computes its own
// globally-unique channel index and stores it at that address.
//
// output:
//   mem[0..15] = [0, 1, 2, ..., 15]
kernel void blockidx_test() {
    int tid = threadIdx;
    int bid = blockIdx;
    int val = bid * 4 + tid;
    mem[val] = val;
}
